# Claude Code project state (per-machine, not part of the wiki)
.claude/

# Project-root scratch notes (residual personal-setup material distilled out of
# wiki/notes/ that isn't appropriate for the canonical wiki). Per-machine, not tracked.
/notes/

# Drift-check working directory. `scripts/check_source_drift.py --check` saves a
# drifted download here as evidence rather than discarding it (re-fetching a 38 MB
# annual report to look at the diff twice is wasteful). Per-machine, not tracked.
.drift/

# Python bytecode from scripts/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Obsidian volatile state — per-machine workspace + cache.
# Vault config (app.json, appearance.json, core-plugins.json) is kept tracked
# at wiki/.obsidian/, which is the canonical vault. A project-root .obsidian/
# is treated as accidental (Obsidian opened against the wrong directory) and
# ignored entirely.
wiki/.obsidian/workspace.json
wiki/.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
wiki/.obsidian/cache
wiki/.obsidian/graph.json
wiki/.obsidian/plugins/*/data.json
/.obsidian/

# Obsidian untitled/scratch canvases
wiki/Untitled.canvas

# Duplicate raw sources — deliberate exclusions, NOT a blanket raw/ rule.
# raw/ is the immutable source archive and its PDFs are normally committed;
# these specific files are near-identical copies of something already archived,
# excluded to keep the repo (and the slow pushes) smaller. Each one has its
# dedup rationale recorded in wiki/log.md.
#
# arXiv v4 of the Cosmos 3 technical report (2026-06-24, 28 MB).
#
# NOTE (2026-08-29): the rationale that first put this line here was WRONG. The
# 2026-07-21 hand diff concluded v4 was "no substantive change" against the
# 2026-06-01 lab PDF. It is not — v4 adds MolmoSpaces as a third policy benchmark
# and strengthens a generality claim. The equivalent content is now committed as
# raw/cosmos3-technical-report-2026-06-22.pdf (the lab edition, same content), so
# this arXiv-hosted duplicate stays excluded on genuine dedup grounds rather than
# on the false premise. See the Edition history on sources/cosmos-3-technical-report.md.
raw/2606.02800v4.pdf
